Here's how to handle each scenario with modern MSTest (3.9+/3.10+):

## 1. Windows-only tests — `[OSCondition]`

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[OSCondition(OperatingSystems.Windows)]
public void Registry_ReadsExpectedValue()
{
    var value = Registry.GetValue(@"HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\MyApp", "Setting", null);
    Assert.IsNotNull(value);
}
```

The test is **skipped** (not failed) on Linux/macOS.

## 2. Skip in CI — `[CICondition]`

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[CICondition(ConditionMode.Exclude)]
public void GpuRendering_ProducesExpectedOutput()
{
    var result = GpuRenderer.Render(scene);
    Assert.IsNotNull(result);
}
```

This skips the test when common CI environment variables are detected (e.g., `CI=true`, `TF_BUILD`, `GITHUB_ACTIONS`).

## 3. Flaky external API — `[Retry]`

```csharp
[TestMethod]
[Retry(3)]
public async Task WeatherApi_ReturnsForecast()
{
    var forecast = await _weatherClient.GetForecastAsync("Seattle");
    Assert.IsNotNull(forecast);
    Assert.IsNotEmpty(forecast.Days);
}
```

The test retries up to 3 times before reporting failure. Use this **only** for genuinely flaky external dependencies — not to mask bugs.

## 4. Cleanup temp files — `[TestCleanup]` or `IDisposable`

```csharp
[TestClass]
public sealed class FileProcessorTests : IDisposable
{
    private readonly string _tempFile;

    public FileProcessorTests()
    {
        _tempFile = Path.GetTempFileName();
    }

    [TestMethod]
    public void Process_WritesExpectedContent()
    {
        FileProcessor.Process(_tempFile);
        var content = File.ReadAllText(_tempFile);
        Assert.Contains("SUCCESS", content);
    }

    // Runs even if the test throws — guaranteed cleanup
    public void Dispose()
    {
        if (File.Exists(_tempFile))
            File.Delete(_tempFile);
    }
}
```

Alternatively, use `[TestCleanup]`:

```csharp
[TestCleanup]
public void Cleanup()
{
    if (File.Exists(_tempFile))
        File.Delete(_tempFile);
}
```

Both `[TestCleanup]` and `Dispose` run **even when the test fails**. The execution order is: `[TestCleanup]` → `DisposeAsync` → `Dispose`.

---

**Summary:** Use `[OSCondition]` for platform gating, `[CICondition(ConditionMode.Exclude)]` for local-only tests, `[Retry(N)]` for flaky externals, and `[TestCleanup]`/`IDisposable` for guaranteed resource cleanup.
